  "tutHome": "Back to home",
  "tutWelcome": "Welcome to the courtyard of the Sleeping Dragon school. Before climbing the mountain, you'll practice with the wooden dummy. I'll guide you.",
  "tutIntent": "This bubble shows what the dummy will do on its turn: a HIGH strike (up arrow) for 4 damage and 2 to your Structure (S). The enemy always warns you before acting.",
  "tutEnemy": "Its Life (red) and its Structure (violet). Bring its Life to 0 to win. Empty its Structure and it becomes Staggered: it loses its action and takes double damage.",
  "tutPlayer": "This is you: your Life, your Structure, your current stance (Horse) and your Guard, the shield on the right.",
  "tutHand": "Your hand. The number at the top left of each card is its Breath cost. You have 3 per turn, and whatever you don't spend is lost. Press and hold a card to read it; underlined words can be tapped.",
  "tutPlayFist": "Tap Full Punch once to see what it does, and again to play it.",
  "tutDefend": "Now defend yourself. The dummy will strike HIGH, and Step Back gives high Guard. If the height matches and your Guard is enough, you deflect the strike. Play it with two taps.",
  "tutKick": "You're now in Empty stance, where kicks cost 1 less: Whip Kick is free now. Play it.",
  "tutForms": "Full Punch and Whip Kick are the first two steps of Little Red Fist. Complete a form in order and a big strike is unleashed. Defenses don't interrupt it.",
  "tutEndTurn": "Your Guard is ready. End the turn and see what happens.",
  "tutDeflect": "Deflect! You took no damage, the dummy lost Structure and is Staggered: it loses its action and takes double. The deflection also gives you extra Breath this turn.",
  "tutActions": "Two aids: T-Step changes your stance for 1 Breath, once per turn. Breathe charges when you deflect, complete a form, or end the turn with unspent Breath; when you use it, you choose: change your hand, recover Breath, or recover Structure.",
  "tutFree": "Now finish it yourself. While it's Staggered, every strike counts double.",
  "tutDone": "Well done! On the mountain, after each combat you add a card to your deck. Life doesn't recover on its own, only at the fountain. Halfway up, the Shrine offers you two paths. And always check the bubble before you play.",
