  "illStancesTitle": "Stances",
  "illStanceMabuPro": "Fists and palms +2. You take half Structure damage.",
  "illStanceMabuCon": "Kicks cost 1 more.",
  "illStanceGongbuPro": "Fists +3 damage and +1 Structure.",
  "illStanceGongbuCon": "You take 2 more Structure damage.",
  "illStanceXubuPro": "Kicks: cost 1 less and hit +2. Deflecting gives +1 extra Breath.",
  "illStanceXubuCon": "Defenses give 2 less Guard.",
  "illTurnTitle": "Order of a turn",
  "illTurn1": "Your Guard resets to 0, you draw cards and recover your Breath.",
  "illTurn2": "You play cards: tap one to see what it does, and again to play it.",
  "illTurn3": "You end your turn: the cards left over are discarded.",
  "illTurn4": "The foe does what its bubble announced and announces the next move.",
  "illBrokenTitle": "Staggered",
  "illBroken": "If the foe's Structure hits 0, it loses its next action and takes double damage until the end of your next turn. If it happens to you, you start your next turn with 2 less Breath.",
  "illFormsTitle": "Forms",
  "illForms": "Fixed sequences of cards. Play them in order and the last step triggers the form's effect (a strike, Breath, healing…). An attack out of order interrupts it; defenses and techniques don't. On the climb, you learn them as rewards.",
  "lesStrike1": "Welcome. This is turn-based combat: you're on the left, and the wooden dummy is your foe. On your turn you play cards; then the foe takes its turn. I'll explain everything, step by step.",
  "lesStrike2": "This is you. The green bar is your Life: if it reaches 0, you lose. The violet one is your Structure, your balance: you'll see what it's for later on.",
  "lesStrike3": "This is your foe: its name, its Life (red) and its Structure (violet). To win, bring its Life to 0.",
  "lesStrike4": "These are your cards: your hand. Each turn you draw 5 new cards from your deck.",
  "lesStrike5": "Here's how to read a card. Top left, its cost; top right, its type. In the center, the name in English with a drawing of the move (or its Chinese name). At the bottom, what it does: the red bolt is Life damage and the violet hexagon is Structure damage. If it shows → and a stance, it leaves you in that stance after acting.",
  "lesStrike6": "These dots are your Breath, your energy for the turn. You have 3, and each card costs what its circle says. Whatever you don't spend is lost when the turn ends.",
  "lesStrike7": "Tap Firm Punch just ONCE.",
  "lesStrike8": "This is the preview: it shows exactly what will happen, with every bonus already added. To play the card, tap it again.",
  "lesStrike9": "Hit! You took 7 Life (5 from the card + 2 for being in Horse stance) and 2 Structure. Watch its bars drop. Your Breath went from 3 to 2.",
  "lesStrike10": "Now Palm Push: it does little damage but takes a lot of Structure. Tap it twice.",
  "lesStrike11": "You have 1 Breath left: play the other Firm Punch.",
  "lesStrike12": "You're out of Breath. Cards you can't pay for are dimmed: Whip Kick costs 2 in Horse stance. The cards you didn't play are discarded when the turn ends.",
  "lesStrike13": "Before you end, look at this bubble: it's what the foe will do on its turn. The arrow → is the height (MID), 5 is the damage to your Life and S 2 the damage to your Structure. The foe always warns you before acting.",
  "lesStrike14": "You don't have any defenses yet, so it's going to hit you. Tap End turn and watch.",
  "lesStrike15": "It hit you: the red number was the damage to your Life, 5. Your Structure dropped only 1 because in Horse you take half. In the next lesson you'll learn to defend yourself.",
  "lesStrike16": "Your turn 2 has begun: you drew 5 new cards and your Breath is back to 3. That's how every turn starts.",
  "lesStrike17": "The dummy has 10 Life left. Finish it off yourself: pick whichever cards you like.",
  "lesDefend1": "The most important thing in the game: reading the foe's bubble. The arrow is the HEIGHT of the hit: ↑ high, → mid, ↓ low. The number is the damage and S the damage to your Structure.",
  "lesDefend2": "Defense cards give you Guard: a shield that absorbs the foe's hit. Each defense protects one HEIGHT. The dummy will strike HIGH, and High Block protects up top with 9 Guard.",
  "lesDefend3": "Play it: two taps.",
  "lesDefend4": "This is your Guard: 9, high. If the hit comes at the same height and your Guard is enough to cover it, you DEFLECT it (化): you take nothing, the foe loses 3 Structure and you gain 1 Breath for your next turn.",
  "lesDefend5": "With the Breath you have left, hit it: Firm Punch.",
  "lesDefend6": "End the turn and watch.",
  "lesDefend7": "Deflection! You took no damage and its Structure dropped 3. This is fighting well: read the bubble and answer at the right height.",
  "lesDefend8": "Your Guard is back to 0: it only lasts through the foe's turn, so you have to defend every turn. And notice you have 4 Breath: +1 for the deflection.",
  "lesDefend9": "Now a MID (→) hit is coming for 6 damage, and the only defense you have is LOW.",
  "lesDefend10": "Play Low Block anyway, to see what happens at the wrong height.",
  "lesDefend11": "End the turn.",
  "lesDefend12": "Wrong height: Guard absorbed only half and you took 3 damage. Height matters as much as the number.",
  "lesDefend13": "Every foe has a rule of its own. Tap the foe's name whenever you want to read it.",
  "lesDefend14": "Now a LOW (↓) hit is coming and you have Low Block. Defend well and finish it off.",
  "lesStances1": "You're always in one of three stances: Horse 马步, Bow 弓步 or Empty 虚步. Right now you're in Horse. The stance you're IN changes how hard your cards hit and how much they cost.",
  "lesStances2": "Here's what each stance gives. You can see it again anytime from the pause menu, under \"How to play\".",
  "lesStances3": "Tap Lunge Punch once and look at the preview.",
  "lesStances4": "Look at the damage: 8 with a green ▲. The base card does 6, but you strike from Horse, which adds +2 to fists: the ▲ marks what the stance adds, and above it says \"+2 damage from Mǎbù\". If a stance takes something away, you'll see a red ▼. Below, → Bow is the stance it leaves you in AFTER striking. Play it.",
  "lesStances5": "Now you're in Bow: fists hit +3 and take +1 Structure. The card that brought you here didn't use that edge: the NEXT one does.",
  "lesStances6": "Look at Firm Punch: before it showed 7 damage and 2 Structure; now, 8 and 3. Your card numbers always show what they hit from the stance you're in. It strikes from Bow and then leaves you in Horse. Play it.",
  "lesStances7": "That's the trick: a card with → sets up the next one. Before playing, think about the order: first the one that leaves you in the stance the other one uses.",
  "lesStances8": "If no card leaves you in the stance you need, T-Step changes it NOW, for 1 Breath, once per turn. Kicks shine in Empty: tap it and choose Empty.",
  "lesStances9": "In Empty, kicks cost 1 less and hit +2: Whip Kick now costs 0 (the cost turns green) and does 7 ▲. Play it.",
  "lesStances10": "Finish the fight however you like. Before each card, check which stance you're in and which one it leaves you in.",
  "lesStructure1": "This dummy has little Structure: 8. Every attack has two numbers: the red bolt is Life damage and the violet hexagon is Structure damage. If the foe's Structure reaches 0, it becomes STAGGERED.",
  "lesStructure2": "Palm Push barely does damage, but it takes 4 Structure. Play it.",
  "lesStructure3": "Again: it has 4 left.",
  "lesStructure4": "Staggered! See the stars. It loses the action it announced and takes DOUBLE damage until the end of your next turn.",
  "lesStructure5": "Take advantage: Firm Punch. The preview already shows double damage.",
  "lesStructure6": "Its bubble said it was going to cover up (the foe's Guard absorbs the Life damage of your hits, but not Structure). Now it's dimmed: it loses that action.",
  "lesStructure7": "You have Structure too. If the foe empties it, you start your next turn with 2 less Breath. Defending well protects it.",
  "lesStructure8": "End the turn.",
  "lesStructure9": "It lost its action. Now it announces Charge (the lightning icon): on its turn it won't attack you; it gathers strength and its next hit will do 4 more. When you see a charge, get ready.",
  "lesStructure10": "It stays staggered for this whole turn: your hits count double. Finish it.",
  "lesForms1": "A form (套路) is a fixed sequence of cards. Play them in order and, when you complete the last step, an extra strike is added. This one is Little Red Fist: Lunge Punch → Whip Kick → Block and Counter → Step Back.",
  "lesForms2": "First step: Lunge Punch.",
  "lesForms3": "Second step: Whip Kick.",
  "lesForms4": "Two steps marked. Progress isn't lost when the turn ends: the form waits for you.",
  "lesForms5": "Tap Palm Push ONCE, without playing it.",
  "lesForms6": "See the warning triangle: an attack (fist, palm or kick) that isn't the next step INTERRUPTS the form, and you have to start over. Defenses and techniques never interrupt it.",
  "lesForms7": "The third step costs 2 and you have 1 Breath left. End the turn: the form waits for you.",
  "lesForms8": "Third step: Block and Counter, a defense that also strikes.",
  "lesForms8b": "You have 1 Breath left: not enough to Breathe and play Step Back. End the turn; the form waits for you.",
  "lesForms9": "Step Back is missing and it's not in your hand. Tap Breathe and choose «Change hand»: it discards your hand and draws the same number of cards (at least 3) for 1 Breath. It uses one charge; it recharges when you deflect, close forms or save Breath. Use it.",
  "lesForms10": "There it is! Last step: Step Back.",
  "lesForms11": "Form complete! On top of the card's effect: 14 damage, 6 Structure, and you draw 2 cards. On the climb, you learn forms as rewards for winning fights.",
  "lesForms12": "Finish the fight.",
  "lesClimbSlide1Title": "The mountain",
  "lesClimbSlide1": "Each stage is a trail of 13 rooms up the mountain. After each room you choose between two or three doors, and each fight shows what reward lies on the other side. The altitude bar shows how far you've climbed and where the guardian, the fountain and the boss await.",
  "lesClimbSlide2Title": "The doors",
  "lesClimbSlide2": "Each seal is a place: a common fight (武), the guardian or a detour with a strong foe who drops a talisman (精), the boss (龙), the fountain (泉), the shrine (庙), an event (缘), the wandering master (师) and the merchant (商). You can't dodge every fight: the trail always puts foes in your way.",
  "lesClimbSlide3Title": "The chest",
  "lesClimbSlide3": "When you win a room, its chest opens with the reward the door showed. If it's scrolls, you choose ONE thing: 1 of 3 cards for your deck, learn the form on offer, or nothing. You start with no forms: each one you learn stays for the whole climb and has its own effect (a strike, Breath, healing…). A bigger deck isn't always better: your best cards come up less often.",
  "lesClimbSlide4Title": "Life and Structure",
  "lesClimbSlide4": "Your Life does NOT recover between rooms: guard it. You heal at the fountain, with tea (a reward from some doors or the merchant), with some talismans and by breathing deep after clearing a stage. Structure does come back in full every fight.",
  "lesClimbSlide5Title": "The shrine",
  "lesClimbSlide5": "Halfway up you choose a Path: Tiger, Snake or Crane. The Tiger draws more cards and has its own cards and Tiger Fist, which only show up as rewards if you follow its Path. The Snake and the Crane can RETAIN cards at the end of the turn: those cards are kept and you still draw a full hand. The Snake is also offered Snake Fist.",
  "lesClimbSlide6Title": "Up you go!",
  "lesClimbSlide6": "If you lose all your Life, that disciple doesn't return: the school sends another novice, who starts from scratch. Always check the foe's bubble before playing. Good luck!",
